- Authority read: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-pit-canslim-strategy-diagnosis-design.md`.

### Plan conflict/interface scan

| Tasks | Shared file/interface | What one produces vs. consumes | Scan result / ruling |
|---|---|---|---|
| T1 ↔ T2 | `core/pit_diagnosis/models.py`, rulebook loader | T1 defines immutable rulebook types and SHA; T2 extends models with partitions/catalog identities | Clean: T2 must preserve frozen mappings and rulebook hash identity. |
| T1 ↔ T3 | rule IDs `N.*`, `E.*`; fidelity outcomes | T1 declares N one-of and proper-base rule records; T3 supplies causal pattern outcomes | Clean: proper-base/new-high evidence may satisfy N.NEWNESS without catalyst. |
| T1 ↔ T4 | rulebook schema/hash; fact rows | T1 defines evidence observability; T4 stores only rule inputs and immutable provenance | Clean: cache stores no outcome or leader labels. |
| T1 ↔ T5 | rulebook identity | T5 baseline verifier binds the rulebook-free historical authority to the diagnosis identity | Clean: baseline reproduction precedes diagnosis; mismatch is controller error. |
| T1 ↔ T6 | `RuleOutcome`, `FidelityAssessment` | T6 evaluates rules and blocks promotion on unavailable required evidence | Clean: diagnostics may be incomplete but never promotable. |
| T1 ↔ T7 | rulebook publication | T7 publishes canonical rulebook/hash and fidelity label | Clean: publication is derivative, not a second metrics authority. |
| T1 ↔ T8/T9 | closed rule/evidence schemas | T8/T9 expose bounded rule records and outcomes to agents | Clean: agents never receive raw facts or rulebook mutation authority. |
| T2 ↔ T6 | catalog and experiment identities | T2 freezes D0–D5; T6 executes only catalog-defined experiments | Clean: D5 is controller-composed only after measured parents. |
| T2 ↔ T7 | partitions/catalog artifacts | T7 publishes partition identity and catalog hash | Clean: 2025 remains locked evaluation, not an unseen holdout. |
| T2 ↔ T9 | experiment IDs/routes | T9 permits only controller-enumerated experiment IDs | Clean: reasoner cannot invent a strategy change. |
| T3 ↔ T4 | RS snapshots and proper-base evidence | T3 exposes causal helpers; T4 materializes their results from pre-event history | Clean: event-day fields use history strictly before the event. |
| T3 ↔ T6 | pattern and entry contracts | T6 reuses fact-derived masks for D2 entry experiments | Clean: no generic prior-high pass-through is admitted as proper-base evidence. |
| T3 ↔ T7 | evidence artifacts | T7 publishes summarized pattern/funnel evidence only | Clean: raw price histories remain local. |
| T4 ↔ T5 | bundle/cache provenance | T5 verifies the corrected replay; T4 verifies bundle/rule/calendar before cache resume | Clean: any identity mismatch invalidates checkpoint/resume. |
| T4 ↔ T6 | read-only SQLite cache | T6 opens finalized cache read-only and checkpoints experiments separately | Clean: cache build is the sole fact materialization authority. |
| T4 ↔ T7 | cache manifest/checkpoints | T7 records cache hash and atomically publishes diagnosis outputs | Clean: partial cache/output cannot be published as final. |
| T5 ↔ T6 | baseline reproduction | T6 D0 must match T5 immutable authority before other experiments run | Clean: baseline mismatch stops diagnosis. |
| T5 ↔ T7 | baseline artifact set | T7 publishes reproduction status and exact hashes | Clean: verifier streams large files rather than loading them into memory. |
| T6 ↔ T7 | metrics/results schema | T6 computes all evidence; T7 serializes it without recomputation | Clean: harness remains the only metrics authority. |
| T6 ↔ T8/T9 | closed evidence and experiment results | T8 protocol and T9 gate consume summarized T6 outputs | Clean: agents select/rank only; controller runs and measures experiments. |
| T7 ↔ T8/T9 | manifest/event publication | T8/T9 bind agent events to one immutable diagnosis run | Clean: provider payloads stay audit-only and sanitized events are derivatives. |
| T8 ↔ T9 | `PitRoute`, `PitReasoningPlan`, dispatch/parser | T8 adds protocol; T9 adds quarantined gate and preserves existing gates byte-for-byte | Clean: additive dispatch only; no legacy prompt/behavior changes. |
| T9 ↔ T10 | CLI/docs/verification | T10 verifies the gate and documents the completed deliverable | Clean: no paid call, source apply, promotion, or live side effect. |

